## Approval gate
- A feature is built only when the user has set `Status: approved` in `docs/requirements.md`, `docs/architecture.md` and that feature's own `docs/features/e-N-<slug>/requirements.md`. Until then no code, tests or configuration are written for it. Agents never set it and never edit an approved document. Check: `.claude/scripts/check-approval.sh` (all documents) or `--for E-N` (one feature).

## Requirements
- Solution: docs/requirements.md (overview: goal, scope, shared domain, feature index, applied baseline)
- Features: one requirements file per feature (= epic): docs/features/e-N-<slug>/requirements.md, with its user stories
- Applied baseline: BL-API-*, BL-SEC-*, BL-A11Y-*, BL-OPS-*, BL-TEST-*, BL-FLOW-*
- Overrides and exclusions (each with a reason):
  - <none yet>

## Task board (Ordna)
- Tasks are markdown files in `tasks/` (`ordna list`, `ordna show <id>`); config in `.ordna/config.yaml`; upstream agent guide in `AGENTS.md`.
- Hierarchy: epic (`E-N`, = a feature with its own requirements file) > user story (`US-N`) > task (`dev`, `verify`, `defect`), by tags and `depends_on`. See the `ordna-tasks` skill; it wins over `AGENTS.md`.
- Every agent claims its task before starting, updates it as the work changes state, and never marks its own work `done`. Nobody runs `ordna commit`; the lead commits.
- Check: `.claude/scripts/check-board.sh` (installed by the kit).

## Documents (one authoritative file each)
- Build specification: docs/architecture.md (design, API contract, ADRs, slice plan)
- TDD evidence: docs/tdd-log.md
- Test plan: docs/test-plan.md
- arc42 (optional, summarises architecture.md): docs/arc42/

